DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaddddccoomm driver provides support for Addonics FlexPort 8/S (and proba‐
     bly FlexPort 4/S) boards that multiplex together up to eight (or four)
     EIA RS-232C (CCITT V.28) communications interfaces.

     Each aaddddccoomm device is the master device for up to eight ccoomm devices.  The
     kernel configuration specifies these ccoomm devices as slave devices of the
     aaddddccoomm device, as shown in _S_Y_N_O_P_S_I_S.  The slave ID given for each ccoomm de‐
     vice determines which bit in the interrupt multiplexing register is
     tested to find interrupts for that device.  The port specification for
     the aaddddccoomm device is used to compute the base addresses for the ccoomm sub‐
     devices.  The port for the interrupt multiplexing register is fixed, so
     it is doubtful that more than one aaddddccoomm can be used in a machine.

